# What must pass before main takes a merge. github-guard reads this from the
# default branch on the server and applies it to branch protection.
#
#   ci-ok   ci.yml: the one always-run gate. It fails when any job it needs
#           failed, was cancelled or was skipped -- lint, runner unit tests,
#           the state-machine test, config validation, and the Windows smoke
#           test that mounts a WinFsp memfs volume through run-tests.sh over
#           SSH -- or when a job exists that it does not wait for.
#
# Requiring the gate rather than each job means a job can be renamed, split or
# made conditional without leaving a required check that never reports, which
# would block every pull request with nothing to point at.
ci-ok
